# Water-bundled terminal database entry.
#
# Named "alacritty" because Water embeds alacritty_terminal and its
# `tty::setup_env` selects TERM=alacritty when this entry is discoverable
# through TERMINFO_DIRS. Derived from the official alacritty terminfo
# (https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty, Apache-2.0).
#
# `clear` deliberately stays the standard \E[H\E[2J: zle's Ctrl-L
# (clear-screen) and /usr/bin/clear read the same capability, and Ctrl-L
# must keep pushing the current screen into scrollback (alacritty's ESC[2J
# semantics) instead of erasing history. The "clear also erases scrollback"
# behavior is provided separately by Water's zsh integration, which wraps
# the `clear` command and appends raw CSI 3 J (the `E3` capability below
# is advertised for tput users; older tic builds drop it). Same division
# as kitty: plain terminfo + shell-integration-level scrollback erase.
#
# Compile with: tic -x -o assets/terminfo assets/terminfo/alacritty.src.terminfo

alacritty|alacritty terminal emulator,
    use=xterm-256color,
    AX,
    XT,
    E3=\E[3J,
    Smulx=\E[4\:%p1%dm,
    Sync=\E[?2026%?%p1%{1}%-%tl%eh%;,
    Cs=\E]12;%p1%s\007,
    Cr=\E]112\007,
    Ms=\E]52;%p1%s;%p2%s\007,
    Se=\E[2 q,
    Ss=\E[%p1%d q,
    kxIN=\E[I,
    kxOUT=\E[O,
